(380, 'What is the Ministry of MSME\'s role?', 'The Ministry of MSME oversees the development and promotion of micro, small, and medium enterprises in India. It creates policies, implements schemes, and supports MSMEs through funding, training, and infrastructure assistance.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(381, 'Can you explain what Udyog Aadhar is?', 'Udyog Aadhaar was a simplified registration process for MSMEs that has now been replaced by Udyam Registration. It allowed businesses to self-declare and register online for government benefits.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(382, 'Why is the term \'Micro\' used in the context of MSME?', 'The term \'Micro\' refers to the smallest category in MSMEs, typically defined by low investment and turnover thresholds. It helps the government provide targeted support to very small businesses.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(383, 'How does the Ministry of Micro differ from the Ministry of MSME?', 'There is no separate Ministry of Micro. The Ministry of MSME handles all micro, small, and medium enterprises under one umbrella, including policies, classifications, and schemes for micro-level businesses.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(384, 'I saw a mention of \'fees for Udyam registration file.\' Is there a cost involved?', 'No, Udyam Registration is completely free of cost. Businesses can register themselves on the official portal without any fees or intermediaries.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(385, 'Are any documents needed for the self-declaration during Udyam Registration?', 'No documents are required to be uploaded during self-declaration. However, Aadhaar is mandatory, and information like PAN and GST details may be validated automatically.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(386, 'What advantages does Udyog Aadhaar registration offer to MSMEs?', 'It offered benefits like access to subsidies, eligibility for government schemes, easier access to credit, and protection against delayed payments. These are now offered under the Udyam system.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(387, 'I\'ve heard about \'MSME classification.\' How was it determined in the past?', 'Earlier, MSMEs were classified based on investment in plant and machinery. Now, both investment and annual turnover are considered for classification as Micro, Small, or Medium.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(388, 'Why is the Aadhaar number important for MSME registration?', 'Aadhaar is required for identity verification of the business owner during Udyam Registration. It ensures authenticity and links the registration to the rightful promoter.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(389, 'What is the importance of the \'Udyog Aadhaar number\'?', 'The Udyog Aadhaar number served as a unique identifier for MSMEs to avail benefits. Though now replaced by Udyam Registration Number, it was used to track eligibility for schemes and subsidies.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(390, 'Could you provide more information about the \'MSME sector\' in India?', 'The MSME sector forms the backbone of India’s economy, contributing significantly to employment, exports, and GDP. It includes manufacturing and service enterprises with varying levels of investment and turnover.', 'MSME / Udyam Registration', 'services-msme-udyam-registration', 1, '2026-01-21 10:43:28', '2026-01-21 10:43:28'),
(392, 'What is an LLP Agreement?', 'NA', 'LLP', ',/limited-liability-partnership-registration,', 1, '2026-01-21 11:04:48', '2026-01-21 11:04:48'),
(393, 'What are the tax exemptions under Startup India?', 'NA', 'Startup India', ',/startup-India-Registration,', 1, '2026-01-21 11:17:05', '2026-01-21 11:17:05'),
(395, 'What is the meaning of a Private Limited Company?', 'A Private Limited Company is a privately held business entity with a separate legal identity from its owners (directors and shareholders)', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 08:50:33', '2026-02-07 08:50:33'),
(396, 'What are the minimum requirements?', 'A minimum of 2 shareholders and 2 directors is required. At least one director must be an Indian resident. There is no mandatory minimum paid-up capital requirement; it can even be ₹1 per shareholder', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 08:52:16', '2026-02-07 08:52:16'),
(397, 'What documents are required?', '1.For individuals: Identity (PAN, Aadhaar, Passport for foreigners) and address proof (bank statement, utility bill).\n\n2. For company address: Proof of registered office (utility bill, rent agreement, No Objection Certificate from owner). \n\n3. A Digital Signature Certificate (DSC) for all directors is also essential for online filing.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 08:53:04', '2026-02-07 09:04:17'),
(398, 'What is the registration fee/cost?', 'Total costs vary but generally range between ₹7,000 to ₹25,000+, depending on professional fees and state-specific stamp duty. This includes:\n\n• Government fees: Based on authorized capital (e.g., ~₹5,000 for up to ₹1 lakh).\n• Stamp Duty: Varies significantly by state.\n• Professional fees: For CA/CS assistance (₹2,000 - ₹15,000+).\n• DSC cost: ₹2,500 per director', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:04:58', '2026-02-07 09:04:58'),
(399, 'How long does the process take?', 'With documents in order, it typically takes 7 to 10 working days from start to receiving the Certificate of Incorporation. The timeline includes obtaining DSC/DIN (1-2 days), name approval (2-3 days), and MCA processing (3-5 days)\n\nAt last eveything depend upon the government portals.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:06:03', '2026-02-07 09:06:03'),
(400, 'Which is better: LLP or Private Limited Company?', 'The right choice depends on your goals. A Private Limited Company is better for businesses planning to raise equity funding, scale rapidly, and build a formal corporate image, despite higher compliance costs. An LLP is ideal for professional service firms prioritising operational simplicity, lower compliance (e.g., conditional audit), and flexible profit-sharing.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:07:02', '2026-02-07 09:07:02'),
(401, 'Give me a step-by-step checklist.', '1. Obtain DSC & DIN.\n2. Get Name Approval via SPICe+ Part-A.\n3. File SPICe+ Part-B, the main incorporation form, which also applies for PAN, TAN, EPFO, and ESIC.\n4. Prepare and file e-MoA (INC-33) and e-AoA (INC-34).\n5. Receive Certificate of Incorporation with PAN and TAN from the MCA', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:07:29', '2026-02-07 09:07:29'),
(402, 'Can an Indian citizen register a company in the UK?', 'Yes, Indian citizens can form a Private Limited Company in the UK. It requires a UK-registered office address, and a director can be a non-resident. This creates a separate legal entity in the UK, offering credibility and liability protection for business there.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:09:05', '2026-02-07 09:09:05'),
(403, 'What are mandatory post-incorporation compliances?', '• Within 30 days: Hold first Board Meeting, appoint first auditor, establish a registered office.\n• Within 60 days: Issue share certificates to shareholders.\n• Within 180 days: File for a Commencement of Business certificate (Form INC-20A).\n• Annually: Hold an AGM, file financial statements (AOC-4), and annual returns (MGT-7) with the ROC', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:09:25', '2026-02-07 09:09:25'),
(404, 'My company name was rejected what should I do?', 'If a name is rejected in the SPICe+ form, you typically get one chance for resubmission without extra fees. If rejected again, you must file a fresh SPICe+ form. Ensure proposed names are unique, adhere to naming guidelines, and don\'t resemble existing trademarks or company names.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:11:28', '2026-02-07 09:11:28'),
(405, 'Is GST registration mandatory from day one?', 'No, it is mandatory only when turnover exceeds the threshold (generally ₹40 lakh for goods/services, or ₹20 lakh for special category states). However, it\'s required immediately for certain businesses like e-commerce operators or those involved in inter-state supply.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:12:39', '2026-02-07 09:12:39'),
(406, 'What are penalties for non-compliance?', 'Penalties can be severe and include heavy fines on the company and its officers, and even the disqualification of directors. For example, late filing of annual returns (MGT-7) and financial statements (AOC-4) attracts additional fees based on the delay, and repeated defaults can lead to legal action.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:13:39', '2026-02-07 09:13:39'),
(407, 'How do I choose the right business activity class?', 'You must select a National Industrial Classification (NIC) code that best describes your company\'s primary and secondary economic activities. These codes are reported in the Memorandum of Association (MoA) and SPICe+ form. The Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA) and NIC websites provide full code lists.', 'Private Limited Company', ',/private-limited-company-registration,', 1, '2026-02-07 09:15:33', '2026-02-07 09:15:33'),
(408, 'What is the total cost of OPC registration in India?', 'The total cost of OPC registration in India in 2026 typically ranges from ₹6,000 to ₹15,000, which includes zero MCA filing fees for capital up to ₹15 Lakh, state-specific stamp duty, and expert professional charges.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:13:10', '2026-02-10 11:13:10'),
(409, 'What is the step-by-step process for OPC registration?', 'OPC registration in 2026 is a 100% online, 5-step process via the MCA’s SPICe+ portal, typically taking 7–10 working days from name reservation to incorporation.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:14:23', '2026-02-10 11:14:23'),
(410, 'What are the main advantages of an OPC over a Sole Proprietorship?', 'The main advantage of an OPC over a Sole Proprietorship is Limited Liability protection, which ensures that the owner\'s personal assets (home, car, savings) remain safe even if the business faces debts or lawsuits.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:15:06', '2026-02-10 11:15:06'),
(411, 'Who is eligible to form an OPC? Are NRIs allowed?', 'Any Indian citizen (Resident or NRI) is eligible to form an OPC, provided they are a natural person and have stayed in India for at least 120 days in the preceding financial year', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:15:45', '2026-02-10 11:15:45'),
(412, 'What are the ongoing compliance requirements for an OPC?', 'Ongoing compliance for an OPC includes mandatory Annual Filings (AOC-4 & MGT-7A), Director KYC (DIR-3 KYC), and Income Tax Returns (ITR-6), with heavy daily penalties for even a single day’s delay.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:16:41', '2026-02-10 11:16:41'),
(413, 'What are the ongoing compliance requirements for an OPC?', 'Ongoing compliance for an OPC includes mandatory Annual Filings (AOC-4 & MGT-7A), Director KYC (DIR-3 KYC), and Income Tax Returns (ITR-6), with heavy daily penalties for even a single day’s delay.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:21:00', '2026-02-10 11:21:00'),
(414, 'hat documents are needed for the nominee director?', 'The nominee director must provide self-attested copies of their PAN Card, Aadhaar Card, a recent utility bill (address proof), and a signed consent in Form INC-3.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:21:52', '2026-02-10 11:21:52'),
(415, 'When is an OPC required to convert to a Private Limited Company?', 'In 2026, there is no mandatory requirement for an OPC to convert to a Private Limited Company based on turnover or capital; conversion is now 100% voluntary and can be done at any time to facilitate business growth or investment.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:22:44', '2026-02-10 11:22:44'),
(416, 'Can I get a business current account and GST registration with an OPC?', 'Yes, an OPC is fully eligible for a business current account and GST registration; in 2026, both can be applied for simultaneously during the incorporation process using the integrated AGILE-PRO-S form.', 'One Person Company', ',/one-person-company,', 1, '2026-02-10 11:25:27', '2026-02-10 11:25:27');
